 "$schema": "com.minomobi.cad.assembly#v1",
 "name": "gripper-stroke",
 "_": "Parallel-jaw robot gripper, v4: ISO 9409-1-50-4-M6 flange → NEMA 17 pancake stepper with an integrated Tr8×2 screw → flange nut in a carriage on two Ø6 rods → crossbar with two pivot pins → four 27 mm links on bronze bushings, one above and one below the linear block, on a pin spanning two finger tabs → MGN9 blocks on one rail across the front wall → carriers and pads outside. Thrust collar on the bulkhead. 96 × 67 × 104 mm case, pads to y = 140. The physical stroke: the screw is driven at 5 rpm, a screw mate moves the carriage 2 mm per turn (y = 60.68 open → 74.63 closed in 6.978 turns, 83.7 s), fixed mates carry the nut and the crossbar, and the links swing the fingers in: opening 36 → 0 mm. Sweep with period 83.7 s; beyond it the nut runs on, as it would.",
